{"title": "Sectional Mock #34 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A dishonest shopkeeper sold wheat at &#8377;60/kg, but he gives only 960 gm of the wheat instead of 1 kg while selling. If the actual percentage profit earned by the shopkeeper is 25%, then find the cost price of wheat per kg.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 60 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 960 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 25% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;48", "&#8377;56", "&#8377;50", "&#8377;54"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;48", "&#8377;56", "&#8377;50", "&#8377;54"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price of 960 gm wheat = &#8377;60/kg</p><p>Profit percentage = 25%</p><p>Cost price of 960 gm of wheat = 60*100/125 = &#8377;48/kg</p><p>Cost price of 1 kg of wheat = 48*1000/960 = 50/kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price of 960 gm wheat = &#8377;60/kg</p><p>Profit percentage = 25%</p><p>Cost price of 960 gm of wheat = 60*100/125 = &#8377;48/kg</p><p>Cost price of 1 kg of wheat = 48*1000/960 = 50/kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Suhas, a 3.15 m tall tree, and an 11.25 m tall building are positioned such that their feet on the ground are collinear and the tree is located between Suhas and the building. The tree is located at a distance of 45m from the building. Further, the eyes of Suhas, the top of the tree, and the top of the building fall in one line, and the eyes of Suhas are at a height of 1.8 m from the ground. At what distance (in m) from Suhas is the tree located?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2369;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360;, 3.15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364; &#2324;&#2352; 11.25 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2332;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;/&#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2368;&#2351;/&#2360;&#2306;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2368;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;, &#2360;&#2369;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;, &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375; 45 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;, &#2360;&#2369;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2369;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 1.8 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;, &#2360;&#2369;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "5", "7.5", "9"], "options_hi": ["6", "5", "7.5", "9"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=321 height=291 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24118/image035.png\"></p><p>AB = Suhas = 1.8 m</p><p>PQR = Tree = 3.15 m</p><p>MNO = Building = 11.25 m</p><p>PQ = 3.15  -  1.8 = 1.35 m</p><p>MN = 11.25  -  1.8 = 9.45 m</p><p>RO = QN = 45 m</p><p>Let AQ = BR = 'x' m</p><p>In &#916;APQ and &#916;AMN: </p><p>PQ/AQ = MN/AN</p><p>1.35/x = 9.45/(x + 45)</p><p>x + 45 = 7x</p><p>x = 7.5</p><p>Hence, Suhas is 7.5 m far from the tree. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=321 height=291 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24118/image035.png\"></p><p>AB = Suhas = 1.8 m</p><p>PQR = Tree = 3.15 m</p><p>MNO = Building = 11.25 m</p><p>PQ = 3.15  -  1.8 = 1.35 m</p><p>MN = 11.25  -  1.8 = 9.45 m</p><p>RO = QN = 45 m</p><p>Let AQ = BR = 'x' m</p><p>In &#916;APQ and &#916;AMN: </p><p>PQ/AQ = MN/AN</p><p>1.35/x = 9.45/(x + 45)</p><p>x + 45 = 7x</p><p>x = 7.5</p><p>Hence, Suhas is 7.5 m far from the tree. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two cubes of sides 10m and 12m are melted to form a cylinder of radius 4m. What is the height of the cylinder?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>10m &#2324;&#2352; 12m &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 4m &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64.5m", "48m", "54.25m", "50m"], "options_hi": ["64.5m", "48m", "54.25m", "50m"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of two cubes = Volume of the cylinder</p><p>10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 4 * 4 * h</p><p>1000 + 1728 = 22*4*4*h/7</p><p>2728 * 7/(22*4*4) = h</p><p>h = 54.25m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of two cubes = Volume of the cylinder</p><p>10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 4 * 4 * h</p><p>1000 + 1728 = 22*4*4*h/7</p><p>2728 * 7/(22*4*4) = h</p><p>h = 54.25m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the side of an equilateral triangle is increased by 34%, then by what percentage will its area increase?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 34% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["70.65%", "79.56%", "68.25%", "75.15%"], "options_hi": ["70.65%", "79.56%", "68.25%", "75.15%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Area is directly proportional to the square of side of triangle.</p><p>Increase area: Original area = (Increase side)<sup>2</sup>: (Original side)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase area: Original area = (134)<sup>2</sup>: (100)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase area: Original area = (67/50)<sup>2</sup> = 4489/2500</p><p>Percent increase in area = [(4489  -  2500)/2500] * 100</p><p>= 79.56%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area is directly proportional to the square of side of triangle.</p><p>Increase area: Original area = (Increase side)<sup>2</sup>: (Original side)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase area: Original area = (134)<sup>2</sup>: (100)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase area: Original area = (67/50)<sup>2</sup> = 4489/2500</p><p>Percent increase in area = [(4489  -  2500)/2500] * 100</p><p>= 79.56%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X = 0.732<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">84", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = 0.732<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">84", "options_en": ["1108", "1102", "1112", "1116"], "options_hi": ["1108", "1102", "1112", "1116"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x<sup>2</sup> + 1 = x , then the value of x<sup>12</sup> + x<sup>6</sup> + 1 is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>2</sup> + 1 = x , &#2340;&#2379; x<sup>12</sup> + x<sup>6</sup> + 1 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["1", "0", "3", "2"], "options_hi": ["1", "0", "3", "2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>When, x&#178; + 1 = x</p><p>Then,</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> = -1</p><p>x<sup>6</sup> = 1 </p><p>x<sup>9</sup> = -1</p><p>x<sup>12</sup> = 1 </p><p>Given, x&#178; + 1 = x</p><p>x<sup>12</sup> + x<sup>6</sup> + 1 = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When, x&#178; + 1 = x</p><p>Then,</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> = -1</p><p>x<sup>6</sup> = 1 </p><p>x<sup>9</sup> = -1</p><p>x<sup>12</sup> = 1 </p><p>Given, x&#178; + 1 = x</p><p>x<sup>12</sup> + x<sup>6</sup> + 1 = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>&#160;What annual installment will discharge a debt of Rs. 35910 due in 5 years at the rate of 7% simple interest?</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; 7% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2375;&#2351; 35910 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2342;&#2366;&#2351;&#2327;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.4200", "Rs.4900", "Rs.7700", "Rs.6300"], "options_hi": ["4200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "4900 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "7700 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "6300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>\"</p><p>Ist year 100--->28</p><p>II <sup>nd</sup> year 100---> 21</p><p>IlI <sup>rd</sup> year 100---> 14</p><p>IV <sup>th</sup> year 100---> 7</p><p>V <sup>th</sup> year 100---> 0</p><p>570 --- Rs.35,910</p><p>1--- 63</p><p>100 --- Rs.6,300</p><p>\"</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>\"</p><p>Ist year 100--->28</p><p>II <sup>nd</sup> year 100---> 21</p><p>IlI <sup>rd</sup> year 100---> 14</p><p>IV <sup>th</sup> year 100---> 7</p><p>V <sup>th</sup> year 100---> 0</p><p>570 --- Rs.35,910</p><p>1--- 63</p><p>100 --- Rs.6,300</p><p>\"</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average weight of 45 girls is 50 kg. If the weight of a boy is included, the average weight increases by 800 grams. Find the weight (in kg) of the boy.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>45 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 800 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["77.4", "86.8", "80.5", "91.2"], "options_hi": ["77.4", "86.8", "80.5", "91.2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total weight of 45 girls = 45*50 = 2250 kg</p><p>Total weight of 45 girls and 1 boy = 46*50.8 = 2336.8 kg</p><p>So, the weight (in kg) of the boy = 2336.8  -  2250 = 86.8 kg</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>Total increase in weight = (800/1000) x 46 = 36.8 kg</p><p>Weight of the boy = 50 + 36.8 = 86.8 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total weight of 45 girls = 45*50 = 2250 kg</p><p>Total weight of 45 girls and 1 boy = 46*50.8 = 2336.8 kg</p><p>So, the weight (in kg) of the boy = 2336.8  -  2250 = 86.8 kg</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>Total increase in weight = (800/1000) x 46 = 36.8 kg</p><p>Weight of the boy = 50 + 36.8 = 86.8 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sec 6A = cosec (A - 29&deg;), where 2A is an acute angle, then the measure of &#8736;A = ___&deg;.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; sec 6A = cosec (A - 29&deg;), &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; 2A &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; = ___&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18", "17", "21", "19"], "options_hi": ["18", "17", "21", "19"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>sec 6A = cosec (A - 29&deg;)</p><p>cosec (90&deg; - 6A) = cosec (A - 29&deg;)</p><p>90&deg; - 6A = A  -  29&deg;</p><p>7A = 119</p><p>A = 17&deg; </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>sec 6A = cosec (A - 29&deg;)</p><p>cosec (90&deg; - 6A) = cosec (A - 29&deg;)</p><p>90&deg; - 6A = A  -  29&deg;</p><p>7A = 119</p><p>A = 17&deg; </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of (16<sup>3/4</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(8<sup>5/3</sup> &div; 32).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(16<sup>3/4</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(8<sup>5/3</sup> &div; 32) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2<sup>19/8</sup>", "2<sup>17/6</sup>", "2<sup>8/3</sup>", "2<sup>11/4</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2<sup>19/8</sup>", "2<sup>17/6</sup>", "2<sup>8/3</sup>", "2<sup>11/4</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>= (16<sup>3/4</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(8<sup>5/3</sup> &div; 32)</p><p>= (2<sup>3</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(2<sup>5</sup> &div; 2<sup>5</sup>)</p><p>= 2<sup>3  -  (5/8) + 5  -  5</sup></p><p><b>= 2<sup>19/8</sup></b></p><p><sup> </sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= (16<sup>3/4</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(8<sup>5/3</sup> &div; 32)</p><p>= (2<sup>3</sup> &div; 2<sup>5/8</sup>)(2<sup>5</sup> &div; 2<sup>5</sup>)</p><p>= 2<sup>3  -  (5/8) + 5  -  5</sup></p><p><b>= 2<sup>19/8</sup></b></p><p><sup> </sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If:</p><p><img width=263 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11855/image031.png\"></p><p>then the value of T/5 will be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;:</p><p><img width=\"263\" height=\"45\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11855/image031.png\"> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; T/5 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["35/3", "40", "120/7", "40/9"], "options_hi": ["35/3", "40", "120/7", "40/9"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=263 height=257 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11855/image032.png\"></p><p>So, T/5 = 40/9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=263 height=257 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11855/image032.png\"></p><p>So, T/5 = 40/9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A and pipe B can fill a tank in 25 hours and 50 hours respectively, then find the time it will take to fill 30% of the tank.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 25 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 30% &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5 hours", "8 hours", "7 hours", "9 hours"], "options_hi": ["5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the total capacity of tank = 50 units (LCM of 25 and 50)</p><p>Efficiency of the Pipe A = 50/25 = 2 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of the Pipe B = 50/50 = 1 unit/hour</p><p>Required time = 3/10 * 50/(2 + 1) = 5 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the total capacity of tank = 50 units (LCM of 25 and 50)</p><p>Efficiency of the Pipe A = 50/25 = 2 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of the Pipe B = 50/50 = 1 unit/hour</p><p>Required time = 3/10 * 50/(2 + 1) = 5 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number of pages read by different person in a day is given in the table. What is the average number of pages read by all persons in a day?</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Person</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Pages</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">265</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">322</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">634</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">145</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">189</td></tr></table>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375; &#2327;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375; &#2327;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">265</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">322</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">634</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">145</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">189</td></tr></table>", "options_en": ["298", "300", "311", "315"], "options_hi": ["298", "300", "311", "315"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of pages read by all the students = 265 + 322 + 634 + 145 + 189 = 1555</p><p>Required average = 1555/5 = 311 pages</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of pages read by all the students = 265 + 322 + 634 + 145 + 189 = 1555</p><p>Required average = 1555/5 = 311 pages</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The speed of two trains are in the ratio of x : y. They are moving in the opposite directions on the parallel tracks. The first train crosses a pole in \"a\" seconds whereas the second train crosses a pole in \"b\" seconds. What is the time taken by trains to cross each other completely?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; x : y &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2346;&#2335;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; \"a\" &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; \"b\" &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(ay+bx)/x+y", "(a+b)/(x+y)", "(ax+by)/x+y", "(bx+ay)/(x-y)"], "options_hi": ["(ay+bx)/x+y", "(a+b)/(x+y)", "(ax+by)/x+y", "(bx+ay)/(x-y)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of two trains be xn and yn respectively.</p><p>Now length of the 1<sup>st</sup> train = xn  X  a = anx</p><p>Similarly length of the 2<sup>nd</sup> train = yn  X  b = bny</p><p>When both the trains are crossing each other then total distance travelled by both the trains = anx + bny</p><p>Relative speed of both the trains = xn + yn</p><p>Therefore time taken = (anx+bny)/(xn+yn) = (ax+by)/(x+y)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of two trains be xn and yn respectively.</p><p>Now length of the 1<sup>st</sup> train = xn  X  a = anx</p><p>Similarly length of the 2<sup>nd</sup> train = yn  X  b = bny</p><p>When both the trains are crossing each other then total distance travelled by both the trains = anx + bny</p><p>Relative speed of both the trains = xn + yn</p><p>Therefore time taken = (anx+bny)/(xn+yn) = (ax+by)/(x+y)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sum of squares of first 12 consecutive natural numbers is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2341;&#2350; 12 &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["450", "550", "650", "625"], "options_hi": ["450", "550", "650", "625"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of square of n consecutive natural numbers is given by  - </p><p><img width=133 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image001.png\"></p><p>Sum of squares of first 12 consecutive natural numbers = <img width=176 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image002.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of square of n consecutive natural numbers is given by  - </p><p><img width=133 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image001.png\"></p><p>Sum of squares of first 12 consecutive natural numbers = <img width=176 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image002.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Worker A alone worked for 24 days in Rs. X and worker B alone worked for 36 days in Rs. X. For how many days Rs. X is sufficient to pay A and B together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352; A &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; 24 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; X &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; 36 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; X &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; X &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["15(2/5)", "12(2/5)", "14(2/5)", "11(2/5)"], "options_hi": ["15(2/5)", "12(2/5)", "14(2/5)", "11(2/5)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let amount of money = LCM (24, 36) = Rs.72</p><p>Money charged by worker A per day = 72/24 = Rs.3 per day</p><p>Money charged by worked B per day = 72/36 = Rs.2 per day</p><p>When they work together, charges per day = Rs.5 per day</p><p>So, required number of days = 72/5 = 14(2/5) days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let amount of money = LCM (24, 36) = Rs.72</p><p>Money charged by worker A per day = 72/24 = Rs.3 per day</p><p>Money charged by worked B per day = 72/36 = Rs.2 per day</p><p>When they work together, charges per day = Rs.5 per day</p><p>So, required number of days = 72/5 = 14(2/5) days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A and B can fill a large tub of water in 2.5 min and 3 min respectively and C can carry away 7 liters per min. If all the pipes are open when the tub is full, it is emptied in 45 min, what is the capacity of the tub?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2396;&#2375; &#2335;&#2348; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2.5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; 7 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2361;&#2366; &#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348; &#2335;&#2348; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; 45 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2348; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2350;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8.25 liters", "9.25 liters", "8.50 liters", "9.50 liters"], "options_hi": ["8.25 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "9.25 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "8.50 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "9.50 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>If X is the capacity of the tub, then in 45 min</p> <p>A will pour 45x/2.5 = 18x</p> <p>B will pour 45x/3 = 15x </p> <p>C will take out 7*45 liters </p> <p>Now x + 18x + 15x = 7*45 or x = 9.25 liters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If X is the capacity of the tub, then in 45 min</p> <p>A will pour 45x/2.5 = 18x</p> <p>B will pour 45x/3 = 15x </p> <p>C will take out 7*45 liters </p> <p>Now x + 18x + 15x = 7*45 or x = 9.25 liters</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The diagonals of a rhombus are 14 cm and 48 cm. What is the perimeter of the rhombus?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; 14 cm &#2324;&#2352; 48 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["120 cm", "140 cm", "96 cm", "100 cm"], "options_hi": ["120 cm", "140 cm", "96 cm", "100 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>d<sub>1</sub> = 14 cm and d<sub>2</sub> = 48 cm</p><p>Since,</p><p>Side of the rhombus = &frac12; * &radic;[(d<sub>1</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (d<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;[14<sup>2</sup> + 48<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;[7<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 25 cm</p><p>Perimeter of the rhombus = 4*25 = 100 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>d<sub>1</sub> = 14 cm and d<sub>2</sub> = 48 cm</p><p>Since,</p><p>Side of the rhombus = &frac12; * &radic;[(d<sub>1</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (d<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;[14<sup>2</sup> + 48<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;[7<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 25 cm</p><p>Perimeter of the rhombus = 4*25 = 100 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;If &#945;, &#946; are the roots of the equation 4x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 2 = 0, then the value of&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&#945;<sup>2</sup>", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#945;, &#946; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; 4x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 2 = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; '?' &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&#945;<sup>2</sup>", "options_en": ["45/16", "43/16", "45/32", "43/32"], "options_hi": ["45/16", "43/16", "45/32", "43/32"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>While comparing the given equation 4x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 2 = 0 with standard quadratic equation ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c = 0, we get</p><p>a = 4, b = 3, c = 2</p><p>Now, &#945; + &#946; = -b/a = -3/4</p><p>And &#945;&#946; = c/a = 2/4 = 1/2</p><p>Now, (&#945; + &#946;)<sup>3</sup> = &#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup> + 3&#945;&#946;(&#945; + &#946;)</p><p>(-3/4)<sup>3</sup> = &#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup> + 3(1/2)(-3/4)</p><p>&#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup>= -27/64 + 9/8</p><p>Therefore, &#945;<sup>2</sup>/&#946; + &#946;<sup>2</sup>/&#945;</p><p>= (&#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup>)/(&#945;&#946;)</p><p>= (-27/64 + 9/8)/(1/2)</p><p>= 45/32</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>While comparing the given equation 4x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 2 = 0 with standard quadratic equation ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c = 0, we get</p><p>a = 4, b = 3, c = 2</p><p>Now, &#945; + &#946; = -b/a = -3/4</p><p>And &#945;&#946; = c/a = 2/4 = 1/2</p><p>Now, (&#945; + &#946;)<sup>3</sup> = &#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup> + 3&#945;&#946;(&#945; + &#946;)</p><p>(-3/4)<sup>3</sup> = &#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup> + 3(1/2)(-3/4)</p><p>&#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup>= -27/64 + 9/8</p><p>Therefore, &#945;<sup>2</sup>/&#946; + &#946;<sup>2</sup>/&#945;</p><p>= (&#945;<sup>3</sup> + &#946;<sup>3</sup>)/(&#945;&#946;)</p><p>= (-27/64 + 9/8)/(1/2)</p><p>= 45/32</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of amount received on a certain sum after 6 month and 9 months is 10:11 respectively, when the interest is compounded quarterly. Find the rate of interest.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 10:11 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2340;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2361;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20%", "40%", "10%", "32%"], "options_hi": ["20%", "40%", "10%", "32%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio = [P(1 + R/400)<sup>2</sup>]/[P(1 + R/400)<sup>3</sup>] = 10/11</p><p>1 + R/400 = 11/10</p><p>400 + R = 440</p><p>R = 40%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio = [P(1 + R/400)<sup>2</sup>]/[P(1 + R/400)<sup>3</sup>] = 10/11</p><p>1 + R/400 = 11/10</p><p>400 + R = 440</p><p>R = 40%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The square root of 7 + 2&#8730;10 is</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>7 + 2&radic;10 &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2350;&#2370;&#2354; ___ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["(&#8730;6 + 1)", "(&#8730;3 + 2)", "(&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)", "(2 + &#8730;5)"], "options_hi": ["(&radic;6 + 1)", "(&radic;3 + 2)", "(&radic;2 + &radic;5)", "(2 + &radic;5)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><span>Formula:&#160;(a + b)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;= a</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ b</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ 2ab</span></p><p>7 + 2&#8730;10 = 2 + 5 + 2&#8730;(2 &#215; 5)&nbsp;</p><p><span>= (&#8730;2)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ (&#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ 2&#8730;(2 &#215; 5)</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;= (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span></p><p><span>Square root of 7 + 2&#8730;10 = Square root of (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;= (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><span>Formula:&#160;(a + b)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;= a</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ b</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ 2ab</span></p><p>7 + 2&#8730;10 = 2 + 5 + 2&#8730;(2 &#215; 5)&nbsp;</p><p><span>= (&#8730;2)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ (&#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;+ 2&#8730;(2 &#215; 5)</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;= (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span></p><p><span>Square root of 7 + 2&#8730;10 = Square root of (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;= (&#8730;2 + &#8730;5)</span></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Find the value of (1 + cot A + tan A)(sin A - cos A)(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin A cos A", "q_hi": "<p><div>(1 + cot A + tan A)(sin A - cos A)( <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin A cos A", "options_en": ["1", "-1", "0", "2"], "options_hi": ["1", "-1", "0", "2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=289 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=316 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=392 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=404 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image005.png\"></p><p><b>We know that:</b> (a  -  b) (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + ab) = a<sup>3</sup>  -  b<sup>3</sup></p><p><img width=217 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=24 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image007.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=289 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=316 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=392 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=404 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image005.png\"></p><p><b>We know that:</b> (a  -  b) (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + ab) = a<sup>3</sup>  -  b<sup>3</sup></p><p><img width=217 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=24 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22503/image007.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Average gym attendance for Mon to Fri was 30. If 50 persons attended the gym on Saturday and average of all seven days is 32, then how many persons must attend on Sunday?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2379;&#2350;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2325; &#2332;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; 30 &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 50 &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 32 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["22", "24", "26", "28"], "options_hi": ["22", "24", "26", "28"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Desired 7-day total: 7  X  32 = 224</p><p>Sum for first 6 days: 5 * 30 + 50 = 150 + 50 = 200</p><p>Sunday attendance: 224  -  200 = <b>24</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Desired 7-day total: 7  X  32 = 224</p><p>Sum for first 6 days: 5 * 30 + 50 = 150 + 50 = 200</p><p>Sunday attendance: 224  -  200 = <b>24</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ashu can do a piece of work in 40 days. He completed 5/8 of the work and then left it. Shweta can complete the remaining work in 18 days. If they work together they will complete 110% of the same work in-</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2358;&#2369; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 40 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; 5/8 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 18 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; 110% &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 Days", "16 Days", "24 Days", "28 Days"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;", "16 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;", "24 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;", "28 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Part of work done by shweta in 18 days= 3/8</p><p>So, whole work can be completed by shweta in 18 x 8/3 = 48 days</p><p>Let total work = LCM of 40 and 48 = 240 units</p><p>Efficiency of Ashu = 240/40 = 6 units per day</p><p>Efficiency of Shweta = 240/48 = 5 units per day</p><p>Together they will complete 110% of 240 in [240* (110/100)]/11 = 24 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Part of work done by shweta in 18 days= 3/8</p><p>So, whole work can be completed by shweta in 18 x 8/3 = 48 days</p><p>Let total work = LCM of 40 and 48 = 240 units</p><p>Efficiency of Ashu = 240/40 = 6 units per day</p><p>Efficiency of Shweta = 240/48 = 5 units per day</p><p>Together they will complete 110% of 240 in [240* (110/100)]/11 = 24 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>The numerator of a fraction is increased by 110% and the denominator is decreased by 16%. If the resultant fraction is 4/3, what is the original fraction?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 110% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 16% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 4/3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2/3", "3/8", "5/9", "8/15"], "options_hi": ["2/3", "3/8", "5/9", "8/15"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}]}